19. Dynamic Strategic Playstyles

Create a strategy layer that continuously evaluates the current situation.

Suggested strategic modes:

Rushdown: high offensive pressure, fast approaches, close-range conversions.

Controlled Offense: pressure while maintaining good spacing and escape options.

Balanced Neutral: alternate between approaching, defending, and punishing.

Counterplay: invite an opponent’s commitment and capitalize on mistakes.

Zoning: control space using attacks and projectiles.

Trap Control: restrict opponent movement and capitalize on predictable escapes.

Survival: reduce elimination risk while maintaining useful actions.

Finisher Hunt: seek reliable elimination opportunities.

Recovery: return safely to the stage and regain a viable position.

These are universal strategic states, not character-specific personalities.

The CPU must determine when each mode is useful from the current matchup and available capabilities.

A CPU can transition from survival into offense when a safe punish appears.

A CPU can disengage from offense when its Launch Point becomes dangerous.

A CPU can use a defensive strategy to set up an aggressive counterattack.

Transitions must feel deliberate rather than random.

Avoid repetitive cycles between modes.

